<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Kersaf pre-exep half yr shr up, div rises.</title>
<headline>Kersaf pre-exep half yr shr up, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, post exceps (cts) 168	  vs    167</p>
<p>    Shr, pre exceps (cts)  159	  vs    147</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   83	  vs     80</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast Kersaf's earnings rising to between 169.1 and 173.5 cents with consensus at 170.6 cents from 147.0 cents a year ago.</p>
<p>They put the dividend at between 92.0 and 94.4 cents with consensus at 92.8 versus 80 cents before.  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	  141.9     vs    138.6</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  372.1     vs    367.6</p>
<p>    Tax			 82.3     vs     75.4</p>
<p>    Turnover	     1,383.2     vs  1,360.8</p>
<p>Div payable around April 4</p>
<p>on register March 7</p>
<p>Full name: Kersaf Investments Ltd (beverages, hotels &amp; leisure)</p>
<p>NOTE(2) - The group said trading conditions remained difficult, particularily in the face of illegal casino activity, higher gaming taxes and increasing capacity in the hospitality industry in South Africa.</p>
<p>However, it anticipated that with high growth from offshore operations and the continuing sound performance of City Lodge Hotels Ltd and Interleisure Ltd, earnings growth before exceptional items for the full year would be similar to that achieved for the half year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
